            "review_title": "Review at Bao Khanh",
            "review_text": "G C\nAnchorage, Alaska966 contributions\n0\nUnfortunately, my worst meal in Ha Noi :(((\nApr 2015 • Solo\nAfter reading the good Trip Advisor reviews for the Bao Khanh restaurant, I decided to give this place a try... It has a very good location, just off Hoan Kiem Lake and in the main Old Quarter area. I checked out the menu that was placed outside, and it seemed that they offered a wide variety of items, including many seafood selections, at reasonable prices. I took an upstairs table (nice setting overlooking the streets), and had my order taken by a polite waitress, then awaited the arrival of my food. My heart sank when I saw that the braised catfish appeared to be the same type as you can buy pre-made/frozen at any Ha Noi supermarket -- it was served in the exact same style & size of clay pot... and the first bite confirmed my suspicions (as I've purchased these from the grocery stores, & found them to be only mediocre in taste). The rice included a lot of dried scrapings from the bottom of the steamer pot, and more than half of the container was thus inedible :(( At least the stir fried mustard greens were OK... I hesitated to give the Bao Khanh such a low rating -- perhaps I happened to select the wrong item, or visited on a \"off\" day (?) -- but, sad to say, this restaurant was the worst place that I've eaten at in Ha Noi (out of nearly 50 eateries tried so far)... I hope that other diners will have a better experience than I...\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 26, 2015",
